wt clean - Back up and clean worktrees

Usage: [1m[36mwt clean[0m [36m[OPTIONS][0m [36m<COMMAND>[0m

[1m[32mCommands:[0m
  [1m[36mrm[0m       Back up and remove worktrees
  [1m[36msweep[0m    Back up and remove inactive worktrees
  [1m[36mkeep[0m     Pin a worktree against cleanup
  [1m[36mrestore[0m  Recreate a worktree from backup

[1m[32mOptions:[0m
  [1m[36m-h[0m, [1m[36m--help[0m
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

[1m[32mGlobal Options:[0m
  [1m[36m-C[0m[36m [0m[36m<path>[0m
          Working directory for this command

      [1m[36m--config[0m[36m [0m[36m<path>[0m
          User config file path

      [1m[36m--config-set[0m[36m [0m[36m<toml>[0m
          Override config with inline TOML, e.g. --config-set list.full=true (repeatable)

  [1m[36m-v[0m, [1m[36m--verbose[0m[36m...[0m
          Verbose output (-v: info logs + hook/alias template variables on stderr; -vv: also debug logs and raw subprocess output written to .git/wt/logs/). Set WORKTRUNK_VERBOSE=0|1|2 to apply the same level everywhere — including shell completion, which no flag can reach

  [1m[36m-y[0m, [1m[36m--yes[0m
          Skip approval prompts

Commits are confirmed on the primary remote before removal. Uncommitted work is saved locally; ignored build output is discarded.

[1m[32mExamples[0m

[107m [0m [2m[0m[2m[34mwt[0m[2m clean rm feature/auth[0m
[107m [0m [2m[0m[2m[34mwt[0m[2m clean rm feature/auth [0m[2m[36m--after[0m[2m 10m[0m
[107m [0m [2m[0m[2m[34mwt[0m[2m clean rm feature/auth [0m[2m[36m--wait[0m[2m 5s[0m
[107m [0m [2m[0m[2m[34mwt[0m[2m clean sweep [0m[2m[36m--dry-run[0m
[107m [0m [2m[0m[2m[34mwt[0m[2m clean sweep [0m[2m[36m--all-repos[0m[2m [0m[2m[36m--root[0m[2m ~/code [0m[2m[36m--format[0m[2m json[0m
[107m [0m [2m[0m[2m[34mwt[0m[2m clean keep feature/auth[0m
[107m [0m [2m[0m[2m[34mwt[0m[2m clean keep feature/auth [0m[2m[36m--off[0m
[107m [0m [2m[0m[2m[34mwt[0m[2m clean restore feature/auth[0m

[1m[32mWorktrees and backups[0m

Worktrees are addressed by branch name, with the worktree's own path as an alias resolved after the branch. Omitting BRANCH selects the current worktree where the argument is optional.

Before any removal, commits must be confirmed on the primary remote. Missing commits are pushed to [2mwt-backup/<branch>[0m; detached heads use [2mwt-backup/detached-<worktree folder name>-<first 12 tip SHA characters>[0m. Tracked changes, untracked files, and differing ignored [2m.env*[0m files are saved locally under [2m~/.wt-attic/[0m and never uploaded. Other ignored content, including nested repositories under ignored paths, is discarded. Only [2m.env*[0m files Git can list in the worktree itself are saved. Untracked 
repositories and submodules with unsaved work prevent removal. A missing remote, failed backup, or worktree changed during backup prevents removal.

Primary and pinned worktrees are kept. Locks are respected except factory locks whose reasons start with [2mhc factory run[0m or [2mherdr-factory run[0m. Removal hooks follow the same approval rules as [2mwt remove[0m.

[1m[32mPreview and JSON[0m

[2mrm[0m and [2msweep[0m accept [2m--dry-run[0m: print verdicts and reasons without changing anything. A preview checks file contents, attic safety, submodules, locks, and remote backup status. It may query the remote with [2mls-remote[0m, but never pushes or runs hooks. A [2mwould-remove[0m verdict describes the current checks; a later write, hook, or push can still fail. It does not wait for [2m--wait[0m or start a job for [2m--after[0m.

[2m--format json[0m prints one array. Each item has [2mrepo[0m, [2mbranch[0m (null for detached HEAD), [2mpath[0m, [2mverdict[0m ([2mremoved[0m, [2mkept[0m, [2mdeferred[0m, or [2mwould-remove[0m), [2mreason[0m, [2mbackup[0m ([2mon-remote[0m, the pushed ref, or null), and [2mattic[0m (path or null). In a preview, [2mbackup[0m is [2mon-remote[0m if the tip is already there; otherwise it is null and [2mreason[0m names the ref that would be pushed.

[1m[32mStored files[0m

                            Location                                                          Contents                              
 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── 
 [2m~/.wt-attic/<repo>/<branch, slashes as dashes>/<UTC timestamp>/[0m [2mtracked.patch[0m, [2muntracked/[0m, [2mignored-env/[0m, and [2mmeta.json[0m; local only 
 Beside user config: [2mclean-repositories.json[0m                     Repositories visited by clean commands, except dry runs            
 Beside user config: [2mclean-terminal-history.json[0m                 Terminal turns and the last time each changed                      
 [2m.git/wt/clean/<unique-id>/marks.json[0m                            Pins and remove-requested marks                                    
 Each worktree admin directory: [2mwt/clean-id.json[0m                 Pointer to that worktree's marks                                   
 [2m.git/wt/logs/clean.jsonl[0m                                        Removal results and skipped or failed delayed requests             

Registry and mark updates use sibling lock files. Delayed-job output and remove-hook output use the usual per-branch logs under [2m.git/wt/logs/[0m. Sweeps expire attic entries at least 30 days old. Backed-up commits stay on the remote.

[2mrm[0m exits 0 when every request succeeds or is deferred, 1 on a refusal or failure. [2msweep[0m exits 0 even when individual worktrees are kept; failures of the sweep itself exit 1. [2mkeep[0m and [2mrestore[0m exit 0 on success, 1 on failure. Invalid arguments exit 2.

